{
  "about": "Serial 123 point 7 (amendment 1): an address found in prose ends where its own grammar cannot continue. After the id (or a world alone), `@` and a moment and `?lens=` and a lens continue it; any other query key or a fragment is not part of an address found in prose, and the address ends before its `?`, `&` or `#`. readOwLinkAt(text, index) / read_ow_link_at(text, index) reads the address starting exactly at index: `end` is the index just past it, `address` is text[index:end], and `reading` is what the whole-string parser answers for that slice. null when the text at index is not an address. `index` defaults to 0. Kept byte for byte in both packages.",
